From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: drain NPU poll tails before final IRQ mask

napi_disable() waits for NAPI ownership to be released, not for the poll
callback to return. An NPU RX poll can therefore complete NAPI, race the
second interrupt mask in mt7996_npu_pre_stop(), and subsequently re-enable
its IRQ from rx_poll_complete(). The NAPI state mutex does not serialize
this callback tail.

Wait for the old network read-side sections after all NAPI instances have
been disabled and before the final interrupt mask. The NPU poll holds RCU
across rx_poll_complete(), and npu_stop_mutex prevents post_reset from
restoring the data NAPI instances during this wait.

The common pre-stop also covers terminal quiesce before RX queue cleanup,
so no extra grace period is needed for each queue. The wait is limited to
recovery and teardown, without changing packet processing or adding a
hot-path lock.

Signed-off-by: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 mt7996/init.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mt7996/init.c b/mt7996/init.c
index 5324ff9..21d0797 100644
--- a/mt7996/init.c
+++ b/mt7996/init.c
@@ -2042,7 +2042,10 @@ void mt7996_npu_pre_stop(struct mt7996_dev *dev)
 		mt76_napi_disable(&dev->mt76, MT76_NAPI_TX,
 				  &dev->mt76.tx_napi);
 
-	/* A poll completing during quiesce can re-enable its IRQ. */
+	/* A poll can re-enable its IRQ after releasing NAPI ownership.
+	 * Drain its RCU/BH read-side section before the final mask.
+	 */
+	synchronize_net();
 	mt76_npu_disable_irqs(&dev->mt76);
 	mt7996_irq_disable(dev, ~0);
 	WRITE_ONCE(dev->mt76.mmio.irqmask, irqmask);
